    "finalText": "Everything works now. `node run-tests.js` and `node checks/contract.cjs` (the declared check) both pass.\n\n## What was broken and what I changed\n\n**`src/storage.js`** — `key(tenant, id)` returned just `id`, so tenants shared one namespace (violates tenant isolation). Now returns `JSON.stringify([tenant, id])`, which cannot collide even when tenant/id contain punctuation or delimiters.\n\n**`src/replay.js`** — `replay` filtered to `op === 'put'`, silently dropping deletions during `open(history)`, so replayed ledgers resurrected deleted pairs. Now applies every event in order.\n\n**`src/api.js`**\n- `apply()` now invalidates the read cache for the mutated key, so cached hits *and* cached misses go fresh after every mutation path (put, remove, batch, and replay-time applies).\n- `batch()` previously did `rows.set(...)` directly — it ignored `delete` events, bypassed cache invalidation, and never journaled through `mutate`'s canonical path. It now routes each event through the same `mutate` function, preserving call order and journal integrity.\n\n**`tests/stateful-contract.test.cjs`** (new, wired into `run-tests.js`) — covers the gaps the smoke test missed: cross-tenant isolation with delimiter-hostile names; cached-miss freshness after batch puts; cached-hit staleness after put/batch-delete/remove; batch put/delete ordering; journal order + detached array/events + tamper-resistance; `open(exportJournal())` reproducing deletions; repeated replay equivalence (a→b→c); history preserved for subsequent mutations after replay; and caller's input array not being destructed by `open`.\n\nI left `checks/contract.cjs` and `amabie.project.json` untouched so the declared proof hash remains valid. Amabie reports the repo as NOT CONNECTED; I did not run `setup` since connecting isn't part of this task, and I haven't committed — say the word if you want a local commit."
  },
